        "original_id": "8fa9b9db-a6ff-552d-882a-90d547ea6ab8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kuk Harrell, Rihanna, Beyoncé, Diane Warren, Ryan Tedder, Brent Kutzle, Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Katy Perry, Gwen Stefani\n- Songs: \"Only Girl (In the World)\", \"Umbrella\", \"I Was Here\"\n- Albums: Loud\n- Groups: Destinee & Paris\n- Places: New Jersey, Los Angeles\n- Topics: vocal production, songwriting, musical influences, Grammy Awards, Billboard\n\nFacts:\n- Rihanna released \"Only Girl (In the World)\" on her 2010 album Loud.\n- Kuk Harrell earned his fourth Grammy for vocal production on Rihanna's Billboard number-one single \"Only Girl (In the World)\".\n- Kuk Harrell was the vocal producer and co-writer of Rihanna's Grammy-winning single \"Umbrella\".\n- Diane Warren wrote \"I Was Here\".\n- Ryan Tedder, Brent Kutzle, and Kuk Harrell produced \"I Was Here\", and Beyoncé received vocal production credit for the song.\n- Destinee & Paris were born and raised in New Jersey and later became based in Los Angeles.\n- Destinee & Paris cited Britney Spears, Michael Jackson, Christina Aguilera, Beyoncé, Katy Perry, Rihanna, and Gwen Stefani as musical influences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
